# --- process machinery (see AGENTS.md) ---
# One worktree per writer lives in-repo (never /tmp: in this harness a /tmp write
# can be a per-call tmpfs, so a worktree created there does not exist for the next
# call). gitignored so it never appears in the main tree's status or a build.
worktrees/
# The gate's raw logs. Kept IN THE WORKSPACE on purpose, so a background run's
# evidence outlives the process that wrote it.
.gate-logs/
# The ONE gate lock (mkdir-based, shared by every worktree).
.futuremagic-lock/
